    {
      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "The straight-line depreciation formula is quite straightforward, which is a relief for your year-end reports. You calculate it by taking the cost of the asset, subtracting the salvage value, and then dividing that result by the asset's useful life in years. So, the basic formula is: (Cost - Salvage Value) / Useful Life. This method spreads the cost evenly over the machine's expected lifespan, which is a nice, predictable approach for accounting.",
